            <div xml:id="d123">

                <pb facs="0237" n="117" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg117"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.51/3479: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stafford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-09-04T12:00:00-04:40">September 4,
                        1931—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>55. Your telegram No. 81, September 3, 6 p.m. Law has been passed but not
                    promulgated by President who informs me he is returning it to Congress for
                    amendment. Dunn says in confidence that amendment was proposed by Judge
                        Schoenrich<anchor n="30" xml:id="d123-f1"/> and authorizes President to
                    accept suspension or substantial reduction in sinking fund rate on bonds now
                    outstanding in lieu of $25,000,000 issue if latter is found impossible. Dunn
                    plans to leave on plane Sunday and should be in Washington, Tuesday evening. He
                    will urge President to delay passage and promulgation of amended law until
                    appropriate time.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stafford</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
